---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Counted from the collection so the sentence below cannot go stale.
const NUM = ['zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine', 'ten', 'eleven', 'twelve', 'thirteen', 'fourteen', 'fifteen', 'sixteen', 'seventeen', 'eighteen', 'nineteen', 'twenty', 'twenty-one', 'twenty-two', 'twenty-three', 'twenty-four', 'twenty-five', 'twenty-six', 'twenty-seven', 'twenty-eight', 'twenty-nine', 'thirty', 'thirty-one', 'thirty-two', 'thirty-three', 'thirty-four', 'thirty-five', 'thirty-six', 'thirty-seven', 'thirty-eight', 'thirty-nine', 'forty'];
const lessonCount = (await getCollection('lessons', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).length;
const lessonWord = NUM[lessonCount] ?? String(lessonCount);
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Biochemistrypedia" description="What Biochemistrypedia is, and the rules that keep it honest.">
  <article class="wrap prose-col" style="padding-top: var(--ddp-space-12)">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>An interactive textbook that refuses to make things up.</h1>

    <p>
      Biochemistrypedia is an interactive site for learning biochemistry, built for
      the students working through an introductory biochemistry course. It is free,
      and nobody paid for it. The content comes from material
      Prof.&nbsp;Deppmann already has: twenty years of lectures and the
      book <em>The Molecule Hunters</em>.
    </p>

    <h2>The rules that keep it honest</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No invented molecules.</strong> Every 3D structure is loaded live by accession ID from RCSB&nbsp;PDB (macromolecules) or PubChem (small molecules). Nothing is drawn by an AI, ever.</li>
      <li><strong>No unreviewed figures.</strong> Every lecture slide names the person who checked it for accuracy and copyright, and a slide without a reviewer fails the build — the site literally won't compile. Many slides use AI-assisted illustration; the slide viewer says so, and a slide with a known drawing error carries a note saying what is wrong. The scientist portraits are AI-generated artwork and are labeled that way.</li>
      <li><strong>No borrowed questions.</strong> Every practice and MCAT-style question is written for this site and comes with its answer and an explanation of why. MCAT-style items are original, not real AAMC questions.</li>
      <li><strong>Honest media.</strong> Videos and podcasts are embedded from their source, never rehosted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's not here yet</h2>
    <p>
      The AI tutor and the "talk to a scientist" characters are intentionally not
      built yet. A tutor that is confidently wrong would do real harm, so that
      part waits until it can be grounded in the course material and clearly
      labelled. What is here is the reading: {lessonWord} lessons, each one finished
      before it went up.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope follows the syllabus</h2>
    <p>
      The chapters here are the chapters of Prof.&nbsp;Deppmann's one-semester
      biochemistry course, start to finish. Three sit outside it. An interlude on
      alchemy and vitalism opens the sequence, because the question of what makes
      living matter different from the rest is where the field starts. Two
      supplements close it: nucleotide metabolism, and a survey that puts the whole
      of metabolism back together. None of the three is on the syllabus. They are
      here for anyone who wants to keep going.
    </p>

    <p class="src-meta">
      Code is MIT-licensed and open. Lesson narrative and scientist profiles are
      the authors' intellectual property (see the repository's NOTICE).
    </p>

    <p><a href="/">← Back to lessons</a></p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono);
      font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ddp-color-accent);
    }
    .src-meta {
      color: var(--ddp-color-muted);
      font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
